# Expectation record for 06_control_flow/005_switch_nested_in_loop.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 005_switch_nested_in_loop
area               = 06_control_flow
description        = break and continue interaction between a switch and its enclosing loop, including a loop nested in a case, a switch in a do-while, and nested switches in nested loops
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Free of undefined and unspecified behaviour. Every object (i, j, sum, hits,
loops and the volatile vsel) is assigned before it is read; no read of
uninitialised storage occurs. All arithmetic is on int values with small
magnitudes: the largest accumulated value is 233, far inside the range of int,
so no signed overflow is possible. There are no shifts, no pointers, no arrays,
no unions and no type punning, therefore no aliasing violation and no
dependence on padding bytes. No object is modified twice between sequence
points, and every printf call passes only plain int values already computed by
preceding full expressions, so at most one side effect per argument list. Every
loop has a small fixed bound and every loop that contains a continue inside its
switch increments its induction variable BEFORE the switch, so no loop can fail
to terminate. Evaluation order is never relied upon: each printf receives values
produced by earlier statements, not by side effects within the argument list.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Nothing implementation-defined is observed. Only int values are printed, so the
measured plain-char signedness difference (signed on x86_64 and i686, unsigned
on aarch64 and riscv64) cannot affect the output, and the measured width
difference for long and pointers (4 bytes on i686, 8 elsewhere) is never
exposed because no long, pointer, size_t or ptrdiff_t value is printed and no
sizeof result appears in the output. No address is printed. No floating point is
used. All four targets and all three optimization levels are therefore
compared, and all three oracles are enabled.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
switch_break_in_for sum=19 loops=6
switch_continue_in_for sum=9 hits=4
loop_break_inside_switch=103
while_switch sum=233 hits=5
do_while_switch=10
do_while_switch_continue sum=4 hits=4
nested_switch=41
inner_continue_from_switch=39
END
